A||N||7||kornholio||slow turning signal flash after new battery||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||09-20-1999||04:38 PM||||Does anyone know why my car's turning signals flash extremely slow and sometimes not even at all???  this just happened after I got a new battery.  On friday night, just before it died on the street, the signals wouldn't even flash at all (because the battery was dead). Now with a new battery, I don't understand why it wouldn't be back to normal. Does the alternator have anything to do with it?  The volt light isn't on, so I'm assuming the alternator is fine.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||09-20-1999||06:08 PM||||I assumed that my alternator was fine after I replaced my battery, but it turned out that the alternator was the problem and caused the dead battery. Check it with an accurate voltmeter at the battery with the engine off and then running. The running voltage should be above 13.5||||reg||6
Z||000002||kornholio||09-20-1999||07:03 PM||||If something's wrong with the alternator, the "VOLT" light comes on right?||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||09-20-1999||10:04 PM||||Most of the time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sluppy123||09-20-1999||10:30 PM||||Sometimes it turns on, If It's having a good day||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-21-1999||12:06 AM||||replace the signal can. you may have fried it by trying to run it with 2 low a battery.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WGraffiKs||09-21-1999||04:58 PM||||My CAR ALARM triggers the turn signals when arming or disarming.  The alarm signals are fed to the 4 corners through diodes attached to the turn signal wires.  If these diodes short or become leaky, the signals become extremely slow, and sometimes don't come on at all.  Do you have a similar alarm?  If so, remove the signal wires from the diodes and test the turn signals.  If they become normal, replace the diodes. (you don't live in So. California, do you?  They NEVER use those lights connected to the control arm on the left of the column!)    ;  }||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pat||09-23-1999||02:35 AM||||My turn signals flashed slow...slower...then quit! I replaced the relay under the dash...and PRESTO new quick flashing turn signals.||||reg||1
